    {
      "strategyName": "NDW/Gengar",
      "weather": "Extreme",
      "adventureEffect": "None",
      "difficulty": "3★",
      "text": "<h2>Overview </h2><p>Lunala is a very optimal boss for people intending to start solo raiding with. With a double weakness and enough difficulty to demand energy management, it helps build fundamental use of raiding techniques to solo. It requires a minor/moderate understanding of energy management, and a minor understanding of important strats to consistently pull off wins.</p><h4>Est Time to Win</h4><p>4m 30s</p><p><br></p><h2>Main Strategy</h2><p>The ideal strategy involves initially building boss aggro by usng mega gengar to shoot out 2-3 shadow balls, and then attempting to switch lead after the boss uses its first charge attack. The initial process should go as such</p><p>Mega gengar+2/3 shadow balls-&gt; lunala CA-&gt; swap to either NDW(40 does good enough) or shadow/normal tyranitar with high lvl(40-45 above)-&gt; launch CT attack-&gt; swap lead into NDW(pscyho cut+ tick perfect can help help)-&gt; swap to your catch tanks when boss uses a charge attack-&gt; when out of CT, and lower than 40% hp on lead NDW, relobby with party, but keep NDW as your first lead keeping gengar as your last pic-&gt; continue on.</p><p>Tips</p><p>TPC- Tick perfect casts, used to avoid the energy resolve bug, which can be executed by timing your click at the tick the energy fills the charge bar, which allows you to skip the delayed animation. <a href=\"https://soloraidarchive.github.io/solo-raid-mechanics.html#strategy-tick-perfect-cast\" target=\"_blank\">Tick Perfect Cast</a></p><p>(mega gengar helps when you have little time and hp on NDW, as a mon that can quicky execute the boss in shorter time frames)- <a href=\"https://soloraidarchive.github.io/solo-raid-mechanics.html#strategy-execute\" target=\"_blank\">Execute</a></p><p><br></p><p>Ideally, attempt to avoid the charge move Shadow ball for the boss, since it takes out your best attacker most of the time( NDW) and does not give enough energy to most other applicable mons (tyranitar for example)</p><p><br></p>",
